<title>BELGIUM: Solvay, IBM in Euro systems management JV.</title>
<headline>Solvay, IBM in Euro systems management JV.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian chemicals and pharmaceuticals group Solvay and Industrial Business Machines Corp's  IBM Belgium SA unit want to create a joint venture for the management of Solvay's mainframe and UNIX systems in Europe, Solvay said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Solvay said the joint venture, for which the letter of intent was signed on Tuesday, would be held for 74.9 percent by IBM and 25.1 percent by Solvay.</p>
<p>IBM will be in charge of its operational management and take over all Solvay staff currently handling these operations -- 25 people in Brussels and 15 in Hanover, Germany.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
